.284 47.821C117.22 448 288 448 288 448s170.78 0 213.371-11.486c23.497-6.321 42.003-24.171 48.284-47.821 11.412-42.867 11.412-132.305 11.412-132.305s0-89.438-11.412-132.305zm-317.51 213.508V175.185l142.739 81.205-142.739 81.201z\"></path></svg>\n				</a>\n			</li>\n						</ul>\n			<h2> About Printing Comic</h2>		\n	        			<ul>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">About us</a></li>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Start a Return</a></li>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Contact Us</a></li>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Shipping FAQ</a></li>\n			</ul>\n			<h2>Resources</h2>		\n	        			<ul>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Help Center</a></li>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Delivery</a></li>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Return Policy</a></li>\n					<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Policies</a></li>\n			</ul>\n			<h2>Newsletter</h2>		\n			<h2>Get the latest news, events & more delivered to your inbox.</h2>		\n			<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=\".svg\"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>										<img width=\"358\" height=\"32\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/payment-method.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/payment-method.png 358w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/payment-method-300x27.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 358px) 100vw, 358px\" />													\n			<h2>© 2024 Printing Comics. All rights reserved.</h2>','Footer 1','','inherit','closed','closed','','5064-revision-v1','','','2024-08-27 06:19:21','2024-08-27 06:19:21','',5064,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17662',0,'revision','',0),(17697,2,'2025-07-25 05:09:00','2024-08-27 07:38:40',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','',17697,'','','2025-07-25 05:09:00','2025-07-25 05:09:00','',0,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17697',2,'nav_menu_item','',0),(17706,2,'2024-08-27 07:44:22','2024-08-27 07:44:22','<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we are</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Our website address is: https://printingcomics.com.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Comments</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>When visitors leave comments on the site we collect the data shown in the comments form, and also the visitor&#8217;s IP address and browser user agent string to help spam detection.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>An anonymized string created from your email address (also called a hash) may be provided to the Gravatar service to see if you are using it. The Gravatar service privacy policy is available here: https://automattic.com/privacy/. After approval of your comment, your profile picture is visible to the public in the context of your comment.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Media</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you upload images to the website, you should avoid uploading images with embedded location data (EXIF GPS) included. Visitors to the website can download and extract any location data from images on the website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Cookies</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment on our site you may opt-in to saving your name, email address and website in cookies. These are for your convenience so that you do not have to fill in your details again when you leave another comment. These cookies will last for one year.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you visit our login page, we will set a temporary cookie to determine if your browser accepts cookies. This cookie contains no personal data and is discarded when you close your browser.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When you log in, we will also set up several cookies to save your login information and your screen display choices. Login cookies last for two days, and screen options cookies last for a year. If you select &quot;Remember Me&quot;, your login will persist for two weeks. If you log out of your account, the login cookies will be removed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you edit or publish an article, an additional cookie will be saved in your browser. This cookie includes no personal data and simply indicates the post ID of the article you just edited. It expires after 1 day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Embedded content from other websites</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Articles on this site may include embedded content (e.g. videos, images, articles, etc.). Embedded content from other websites behaves in the exact same way as if the visitor has visited the other website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These websites may collect data about you, use cookies, embed additional third-party tracking, and monitor your interaction with that embedded content, including tracking your interaction with the embedded content if you have an account and are logged in to that website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we share your data with</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you request a password reset, your IP address will be included in the reset email.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How long we retain your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment, the comment and its metadata are retained indefinitely. This is so we can recognize and approve any follow-up comments automatically instead of holding them in a moderation queue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For users that register on our website (if any), we also store the personal information they provide in their user profile. All users can see, edit, or delete their personal information at any time (except they cannot change their username). Website administrators can also see and edit that information.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What rights you have over your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you have an account on this site, or have left comments, you can request to receive an exported file of the personal data we hold about you, including any data you have provided to us. You can also request that we erase any personal data we hold about you. This does not include any data we are obliged to keep for administrative, legal, or security purposes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where your data is sent</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Visitor comments may be checked through an automated spam detection service.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n','Privacy Policy','','inherit','closed','closed','','3-revision-v1','','','2024-08-27 07:44:22','2024-08-27 07:44:22','',3,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17706',0,'revision','',0),(17722,2,'2024-08-27 07:58:16','2024-08-27 07:58:16','<!-- wp:shortcode -->[yith_wcwl_wishlist]<!-- /wp:shortcode -->','Wishlist','','inherit','closed','closed','','17497-revision-v1','','','2024-08-27 07:58:16','2024-08-27 07:58:16','',17497,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17722',0,'revision','',0),(17730,2,'2025-07-25 05:09:00','2024-08-27 08:04:26',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','',17730,'','','2025-07-25 05:09:00','2025-07-25 05:09:00','',0,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17730',1,'nav_menu_item','',0),(17731,2,'2025-07-25 05:09:01','2024-08-27 08:04:26',' ','','','publish','closed','closed','',17731,'','','2025-07-25 05:09:01','2025-07-25 05:09:01','',0,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17731',7,'nav_menu_item','',0),(17743,2,'2024-08-28 10:24:28','2024-08-28 10:24:28','<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=\".svg\"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>										<img width=\"978\" height=\"978\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp 978w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-300x300.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-150x150.webp 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-768x768.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-600x600.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 978px) 100vw, 978px\" />													\n			<h2>Set your files up properly and streamline production.</h2>		\n		<h4><strong>File Prep Package</strong></h4><ul><li>All PDF Printing Comics Templates</li><li>PSD Standard Size Template for your illustrator</li><li>File Prep Checklist</li><li>Setting Up Your Saddle-Stitch Page Count</li><li>File Prep guide sheet and size comparison</li><li>Understanding your bleeds and what not to do</li><li>Why a physical proof helps</li></ul>		\n			<a href=\"#\">\n									DOWNLOAD\n					</a>\n			<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-heading-title{padding:0;margin:0;line-height:1}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title[class*=elementor-size-]>a{color:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-small{font-size:15px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-medium{font-size:19px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-large{font-size:29px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xl{font-size:39px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xxl{font-size:59px}</style><h2>File Setup & Submission</h2>		\n		<h3><strong>Start with the correct template. </strong></h3><p>Properly setting up your files from the beginning can significantly speed up production turnaround time. It starts with your illustrator. Creators and publishers often make the mistake of allowing the initial illustrator to not use a template from the printer intended for the final book. This oversight can lead to critical artwork being cut off when the book is printed—that’s why you need to always review your proofs! We offer over 20 sizes to choose from, accommodating all creative publishing ventures. Moreover, we provide <strong><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">free PDF templates for every size</a>.</strong> Download the appropriate template, share it with your artists, and streamline your production process.</p>		\n													<img width=\"672\" height=\"431\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp 672w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-300x192.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-600x385.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 672px) 100vw, 672px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Size your pages according to your Order. But, dont forget to add bleed. </strong></h3><p>If you are not starting by opening a Printing Comics template in your design software, then you must ensure to add 0.25\" to both the height and width of your file. Chosen size + 0.25\" = File submission size. Correct sizing speeds up the turnaround time.</p>		\n													<img width=\"693\" height=\"563\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp 693w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-300x244.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-600x487.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 693px) 100vw, 693px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Understand your book\'s bleed area, trim line, and safe area.</strong></h3><p>Let’s keep it simple. If you want to print a 6\" x 9\" book, your page files should be 6.25\" x 9.25\". Your artwork should extend 0.125\" past the trim size on all sides of the page. To play it safe, keep all crucial artwork and text 0.125\" within the trim size. Using the Novella example, your safe area would be 5.75\" x 8.75\".</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"640\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-300x208.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-768x532.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-600x416.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Export your files at 300 DPI resolution and CMYK color profile.</strong></h3><p>Ensure your files are exported at 300 DPI resolution and in the CMYK color profile. This will keep your lines crisp and your colors accurate for print.</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"570\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-300x185.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-768x474.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-600x370.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Flatten all of your files.</strong></h3><p>Information can be lost if not embedded. Avoid issues with layers by flattening your files. This ensures all elements are properly incorporated.</p>		\n													<img width=\"988\" height=\"884\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041.webp 988w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-300x268.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-768x687.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-600x537.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 988px) 100vw, 988px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Separate double-page spreads and covers into single pages. </strong></h3><p>Ensure your double-page spreads start on even page numbers. Double-page spreads and covers should be submitted as single pages to maintain order and clarity during the printing process.</p>		\n													<img width=\"790\" height=\"826\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042.webp 790w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-287x300.webp 287w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-768x803.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-600x627.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 790px) 100vw, 790px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Label and share your individual files properly.</strong></h3><p>We currently accept PDFs and JPGs. PDFs can be submitted as single files or combined. If combined, ensure they are in the proper order from cover to back. High-quality files ensure the best print results.<br /><br />If you are not submitting a combined PDF in proper order (from cover to back), then you need to:<br />1. Label each single page PDF or JPG properly. We recommend (Comic Book Title_Page #). <br />2. Combine all files into one folder<br />3. Compress or Zip the folder if needed.<br />4. Upload it  using a file transfer site such as Dropbox, WeTransfer, or Google Drive. <br />5. Share the link to your uploaded files. Be sure the link settings allow anyone with the link to view.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q7inJr71RIs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click Here for a helpful video.</a></p>		\n													<img width=\"942\" height=\"720\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044.webp 942w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-300x229.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-768x587.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-600x459.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 942px) 100vw, 942px\" />													\n		<h2><strong>Ensure you have the correct page count.</strong></h2><p>Saddle-stitch comics should have a page count in multiples of 4, and perfect-bound books should have a page count in multiples of 2. This ensures the structural integrity and proper binding of your book.</p>		\n													<img width=\"998\" height=\"1022\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046.webp 998w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-293x300.webp 293w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-768x786.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-600x614.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 998px) 100vw, 998px\" />													\n			<h2>The Printing Comics Spine Width Calculator</h2>		\n		Getting the spine width right on your perfect bound book can be tricky. But it doesn\'t have to be—with our Spine Width Calculator, simply enter your book\'s specs, and we\'ll deliver precise spine and cover measurements instantly, bleed included. It\'s bookbinding made easy.		\n			<h2>Rep us in your book and save.</h2>		\n		<p>Place our advertisement in your book and receive a discount on your books. You\'ll just need to leave a full page open for our full page Printing Comics ad.</p>		\n			<a href=\"#\">\n									DOWNLOAD\n					</a>\n													<img width=\"811\" height=\"924\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads.webp 811w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-263x300.webp 263w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-768x875.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-600x684.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 811px) 100vw, 811px\" />','File Prep','','draft','closed','closed','','file-prep','','','2024-08-30 03:43:32','2024-08-30 03:43:32','',0,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?page_id=17743',0,'page','',0),(17748,2,'2024-08-28 10:28:17','2024-08-28 10:28:17','','printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates','','inherit','open','closed','','printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates','','','2024-08-28 10:28:17','2024-08-28 10:28:17','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17752,2,'2024-08-28 10:30:30','2024-08-28 10:30:30','','Default Kit','','inherit','closed','closed','','72-revision-v1','','','2024-08-28 10:30:30','2024-08-28 10:30:30','',72,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17752',0,'revision','',0),(17753,2,'2024-08-28 10:30:55','2024-08-28 10:30:55','','Default Kit','','inherit','closed','closed','','72-revision-v1','','','2024-08-28 10:30:55','2024-08-28 10:30:55','',72,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17753',0,'revision','',0),(17754,2,'2024-08-28 10:31:39','2024-08-28 10:31:39','','Default Kit','','inherit','closed','closed','','72-revision-v1','','','2024-08-28 10:31:39','2024-08-28 10:31:39','',72,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17754',0,'revision','',0),(17755,2,'2024-08-28 10:33:52','2024-08-28 10:33:52','','right-size','','inherit','open','closed','','right-size','','','2024-08-28 10:33:52','2024-08-28 10:33:52','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17757,2,'2024-08-28 10:39:15','2024-08-28 10:39:15','','mask-group-115038','','inherit','open','closed','','mask-group-115038','','','2024-08-28 10:39:15','2024-08-28 10:39:15','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17761,2,'2024-08-28 10:45:00','2024-08-28 10:45:00','','mask-group-115039','','inherit','open','closed','','mask-group-115039','','','2024-08-28 10:45:00','2024-08-28 10:45:00','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17765,2,'2024-08-28 10:46:36','2024-08-28 10:46:36','','mask-group-115040','','inherit','open','closed','','mask-group-115040','','','2024-08-28 10:46:36','2024-08-28 10:46:36','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17769,2,'2024-08-28 10:52:37','2024-08-28 10:52:37','','mask-group-115041','','inherit','open','closed','','mask-group-115041','','','2024-08-28 10:52:37','2024-08-28 10:52:37','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17770,2,'2024-08-28 10:53:43','2024-08-28 10:53:43','','mask-group-115042','','inherit','open','closed','','mask-group-115042','','','2024-08-28 10:53:43','2024-08-28 10:53:43','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17771,2,'2024-08-28 10:54:49','2024-08-28 10:54:49','','mask-group-115044','','inherit','open','closed','','mask-group-115044','','','2024-08-28 10:54:49','2024-08-28 10:54:49','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17772,2,'2024-08-28 10:55:42','2024-08-28 10:55:42','','mask-group-115046','','inherit','open','closed','','mask-group-115046','','','2024-08-28 10:55:42','2024-08-28 10:55:42','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17773,2,'2024-08-28 11:01:24','2024-08-28 11:01:24','','group-of-cws-ads','','inherit','open','closed','','group-of-cws-ads','','','2024-08-28 11:01:24','2024-08-28 11:01:24','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads.webp',0,'attachment','image/webp',0),(17775,2,'2024-08-28 11:01:31','2024-08-28 11:01:31','<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=\".svg\"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>										<img width=\"978\" height=\"978\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp 978w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-300x300.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-150x150.webp 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-768x768.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-600x600.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 978px) 100vw, 978px\" />													\n			<h2>Set your files up properly and streamline production.</h2>		\n		<h4><strong>File Prep Package</strong></h4><ul><li>All PDF CWS Templates</li><li>PSD Standard Size Template for your illustrator</li><li>File Prep Checklist</li><li>Setting Up Your Saddle-Stitch Page Count</li><li>File Prep guide sheet and size comparison</li><li>Understanding your bleeds and what not to do</li><li>Why a physical proof helps</li></ul>		\n			<a href=\"#\">\n									DOWNLOAD\n					</a>\n			<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-heading-title{padding:0;margin:0;line-height:1}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title[class*=elementor-size-]>a{color:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-small{font-size:15px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-medium{font-size:19px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-large{font-size:29px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xl{font-size:39px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xxl{font-size:59px}</style><h2>File Setup & Submission</h2>		\n		<h3><strong>Start with the correct template. </strong></h3><p>Properly setting up your files from the beginning can significantly speed up production turnaround time. It starts with your illustrator. Creators and publishers often make the mistake of allowing the initial illustrator to not use a template from the printer intended for the final book. This oversight can lead to critical artwork being cut off when the book is printed—that’s why you need to always review your proofs! We offer over 20 sizes to choose from, accommodating all creative publishing ventures. Moreover, we provide <strong><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">free PDF templates for every size</a>.</strong> Download the appropriate template, share it with your artists, and streamline your production process.</p>		\n													<img width=\"672\" height=\"431\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp 672w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-300x192.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-600x385.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 672px) 100vw, 672px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Size your pages according to your Order. But, dont forget to add bleed. </strong></h3><p>If you are not starting by opening a CWS template in your design software, then you must ensure to add 0.25\" to both the height and width of your file. Chosen size + 0.25\" = File submission size. Correct sizing speeds up the turnaround time.</p>		\n													<img width=\"693\" height=\"563\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp 693w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-300x244.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-600x487.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 693px) 100vw, 693px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Understand your book\'s bleed area, trim line, and safe area.</strong></h3><p>Let’s keep it simple. If you want to print a 6\" x 9\" book, your page files should be 6.25\" x 9.25\". Your artwork should extend 0.125\" past the trim size on all sides of the page. To play it safe, keep all crucial artwork and text 0.125\" within the trim size. Using the Novella example, your safe area would be 5.75\" x 8.75\".</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"640\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-300x208.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-768x532.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-600x416.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Export your files at 300 DPI resolution and CMYK color profile.</strong></h3><p>Ensure your files are exported at 300 DPI resolution and in the CMYK color profile. This will keep your lines crisp and your colors accurate for print.</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"570\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-300x185.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-768x474.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-600x370.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />','File Prep','','inherit','closed','closed','','17743-revision-v1','','','2024-08-28 11:01:31','2024-08-28 11:01:31','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17775',0,'revision','',0),(17776,2,'2024-08-28 11:01:31','2024-08-28 11:01:31','<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=\".svg\"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>										<img width=\"978\" height=\"978\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp 978w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-300x300.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-150x150.webp 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-768x768.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-600x600.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 978px) 100vw, 978px\" />													\n			<h2>Set your files up properly and streamline production.</h2>		\n		<h4><strong>File Prep Package</strong></h4><ul><li>All PDF CWS Templates</li><li>PSD Standard Size Template for your illustrator</li><li>File Prep Checklist</li><li>Setting Up Your Saddle-Stitch Page Count</li><li>File Prep guide sheet and size comparison</li><li>Understanding your bleeds and what not to do</li><li>Why a physical proof helps</li></ul>		\n			<a href=\"#\">\n									DOWNLOAD\n					</a>\n			<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-heading-title{padding:0;margin:0;line-height:1}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title[class*=elementor-size-]>a{color:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-small{font-size:15px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-medium{font-size:19px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-large{font-size:29px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xl{font-size:39px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xxl{font-size:59px}</style><h2>File Setup & Submission</h2>		\n		<h3><strong>Start with the correct template. </strong></h3><p>Properly setting up your files from the beginning can significantly speed up production turnaround time. It starts with your illustrator. Creators and publishers often make the mistake of allowing the initial illustrator to not use a template from the printer intended for the final book. This oversight can lead to critical artwork being cut off when the book is printed—that’s why you need to always review your proofs! We offer over 20 sizes to choose from, accommodating all creative publishing ventures. Moreover, we provide <strong><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">free PDF templates for every size</a>.</strong> Download the appropriate template, share it with your artists, and streamline your production process.</p>		\n													<img width=\"672\" height=\"431\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp 672w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-300x192.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-600x385.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 672px) 100vw, 672px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Size your pages according to your Order. But, dont forget to add bleed. </strong></h3><p>If you are not starting by opening a CWS template in your design software, then you must ensure to add 0.25\" to both the height and width of your file. Chosen size + 0.25\" = File submission size. Correct sizing speeds up the turnaround time.</p>		\n													<img width=\"693\" height=\"563\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp 693w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-300x244.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-600x487.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 693px) 100vw, 693px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Understand your book\'s bleed area, trim line, and safe area.</strong></h3><p>Let’s keep it simple. If you want to print a 6\" x 9\" book, your page files should be 6.25\" x 9.25\". Your artwork should extend 0.125\" past the trim size on all sides of the page. To play it safe, keep all crucial artwork and text 0.125\" within the trim size. Using the Novella example, your safe area would be 5.75\" x 8.75\".</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"640\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-300x208.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-768x532.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-600x416.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Export your files at 300 DPI resolution and CMYK color profile.</strong></h3><p>Ensure your files are exported at 300 DPI resolution and in the CMYK color profile. This will keep your lines crisp and your colors accurate for print.</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"570\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-300x185.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-768x474.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-600x370.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Flatten all of your files.</strong></h3><p>Information can be lost if not embedded. Avoid issues with layers by flattening your files. This ensures all elements are properly incorporated.</p>		\n													<img width=\"988\" height=\"884\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041.webp 988w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-300x268.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-768x687.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-600x537.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 988px) 100vw, 988px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Separate double-page spreads and covers into single pages. </strong></h3><p>Ensure your double-page spreads start on even page numbers. Double-page spreads and covers should be submitted as single pages to maintain order and clarity during the printing process.</p>		\n													<img width=\"790\" height=\"826\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042.webp 790w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-287x300.webp 287w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-768x803.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-600x627.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 790px) 100vw, 790px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Label and share your individual files properly.</strong></h3><p>We currently accept PDFs and JPGs. PDFs can be submitted as single files or combined. If combined, ensure they are in the proper order from cover to back. High-quality files ensure the best print results.<br /><br />If you are not submitting a combined PDF in proper order (from cover to back), then you need to:<br />1. Label each single page PDF or JPG properly. We recommend (Comic Book Title_Page #). <br />2. Combine all files into one folder<br />3. Compress or Zip the folder if needed.<br />4. Upload it  using a file transfer site such as Dropbox, WeTransfer, or Google Drive. <br />5. Share the link to your uploaded files. Be sure the link settings allow anyone with the link to view.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q7inJr71RIs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click Here for a helpful video.</a></p>		\n													<img width=\"942\" height=\"720\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044.webp 942w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-300x229.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-768x587.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-600x459.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 942px) 100vw, 942px\" />													\n		<h2><strong>Ensure you have the correct page count.</strong></h2><p>Saddle-stitch comics should have a page count in multiples of 4, and perfect-bound books should have a page count in multiples of 2. This ensures the structural integrity and proper binding of your book.</p>		\n													<img width=\"998\" height=\"1022\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046.webp 998w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-293x300.webp 293w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-768x786.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-600x614.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 998px) 100vw, 998px\" />													\n			<h2>The Printing Comics Spine Width Calculator</h2>		\n		Getting the spine width right on your perfect bound book can be tricky. But it doesn\'t have to be—with our Spine Width Calculator, simply enter your book\'s specs, and we\'ll deliver precise spine and cover measurements instantly, bleed included. It\'s bookbinding made easy.		\n			<h2>Rep us in your book and save.</h2>		\n		<p>Place our advertisement in your book and receive a discount on your books. You\'ll just need to leave a full page open for our full page CWS ad.</p>		\n			<a href=\"#\">\n									DOWNLOAD\n					</a>\n													<img width=\"811\" height=\"924\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads.webp 811w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-263x300.webp 263w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-768x875.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-600x684.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 811px) 100vw, 811px\" />','File Prep','','inherit','closed','closed','','17743-revision-v1','','','2024-08-28 11:01:31','2024-08-28 11:01:31','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17776',0,'revision','',0),(17777,2,'2024-08-28 11:03:17','2024-08-28 11:03:17','<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=\".svg\"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>										<img width=\"978\" height=\"978\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp 978w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-300x300.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-150x150.webp 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-768x768.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-600x600.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 978px) 100vw, 978px\" />													\n			<h2>Set your files up properly and streamline production.</h2>		\n		<h4><strong>File Prep Package</strong></h4><ul><li>All PDF CWS Templates</li><li>PSD Standard Size Template for your illustrator</li><li>File Prep Checklist</li><li>Setting Up Your Saddle-Stitch Page Count</li><li>File Prep guide sheet and size comparison</li><li>Understanding your bleeds and what not to do</li><li>Why a physical proof helps</li></ul>		\n			<a href=\"#\">\n									DOWNLOAD\n					</a>\n			<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-heading-title{padding:0;margin:0;line-height:1}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title[class*=elementor-size-]>a{color:inherit;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-small{font-size:15px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-medium{font-size:19px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-large{font-size:29px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xl{font-size:39px}.elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xxl{font-size:59px}</style><h2>File Setup & Submission</h2>		\n		<h3><strong>Start with the correct template. </strong></h3><p>Properly setting up your files from the beginning can significantly speed up production turnaround time. It starts with your illustrator. Creators and publishers often make the mistake of allowing the initial illustrator to not use a template from the printer intended for the final book. This oversight can lead to critical artwork being cut off when the book is printed—that’s why you need to always review your proofs! We offer over 20 sizes to choose from, accommodating all creative publishing ventures. Moreover, we provide <strong><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">free PDF templates for every size</a>.</strong> Download the appropriate template, share it with your artists, and streamline your production process.</p>		\n													<img width=\"672\" height=\"431\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size.webp 672w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-300x192.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/right-size-600x385.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 672px) 100vw, 672px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Size your pages according to your Order. But, dont forget to add bleed. </strong></h3><p>If you are not starting by opening a CWS template in your design software, then you must ensure to add 0.25\" to both the height and width of your file. Chosen size + 0.25\" = File submission size. Correct sizing speeds up the turnaround time.</p>		\n													<img width=\"693\" height=\"563\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038.webp 693w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-300x244.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115038-600x487.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 693px) 100vw, 693px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Understand your book\'s bleed area, trim line, and safe area.</strong></h3><p>Let’s keep it simple. If you want to print a 6\" x 9\" book, your page files should be 6.25\" x 9.25\". Your artwork should extend 0.125\" past the trim size on all sides of the page. To play it safe, keep all crucial artwork and text 0.125\" within the trim size. Using the Novella example, your safe area would be 5.75\" x 8.75\".</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"640\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-300x208.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-768x532.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115039-600x416.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Export your files at 300 DPI resolution and CMYK color profile.</strong></h3><p>Ensure your files are exported at 300 DPI resolution and in the CMYK color profile. This will keep your lines crisp and your colors accurate for print.</p>		\n													<img width=\"924\" height=\"570\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040.webp 924w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-300x185.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-768x474.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115040-600x370.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 924px) 100vw, 924px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Flatten all of your files.</strong></h3><p>Information can be lost if not embedded. Avoid issues with layers by flattening your files. This ensures all elements are properly incorporated.</p>		\n													<img width=\"988\" height=\"884\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041.webp 988w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-300x268.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-768x687.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115041-600x537.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 988px) 100vw, 988px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Separate double-page spreads and covers into single pages. </strong></h3><p>Ensure your double-page spreads start on even page numbers. Double-page spreads and covers should be submitted as single pages to maintain order and clarity during the printing process.</p>		\n													<img width=\"790\" height=\"826\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042.webp 790w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-287x300.webp 287w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-768x803.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115042-600x627.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 790px) 100vw, 790px\" />													\n		<h3><strong>Label and share your individual files properly.</strong></h3><p>We currently accept PDFs and JPGs. PDFs can be submitted as single files or combined. If combined, ensure they are in the proper order from cover to back. High-quality files ensure the best print results.<br /><br />If you are not submitting a combined PDF in proper order (from cover to back), then you need to:<br />1. Label each single page PDF or JPG properly. We recommend (Comic Book Title_Page #). <br />2. Combine all files into one folder<br />3. Compress or Zip the folder if needed.<br />4. Upload it  using a file transfer site such as Dropbox, WeTransfer, or Google Drive. <br />5. Share the link to your uploaded files. Be sure the link settings allow anyone with the link to view.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q7inJr71RIs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click Here for a helpful video.</a></p>		\n													<img width=\"942\" height=\"720\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044.webp 942w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-300x229.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-768x587.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115044-600x459.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 942px) 100vw, 942px\" />													\n		<h2><strong>Ensure you have the correct page count.</strong></h2><p>Saddle-stitch comics should have a page count in multiples of 4, and perfect-bound books should have a page count in multiples of 2. This ensures the structural integrity and proper binding of your book.</p>		\n													<img width=\"998\" height=\"1022\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046.webp 998w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-293x300.webp 293w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-768x786.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/mask-group-115046-600x614.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 998px) 100vw, 998px\" />													\n			<h2>The Printing Comics Spine Width Calculator</h2>		\n		Getting the spine width right on your perfect bound book can be tricky. But it doesn\'t have to be—with our Spine Width Calculator, simply enter your book\'s specs, and we\'ll deliver precise spine and cover measurements instantly, bleed included. It\'s bookbinding made easy.		\n			<h2>Rep us in your book and save.</h2>		\n		<p>Place our advertisement in your book and receive a discount on your books. You\'ll just need to leave a full page open for our full page CWS ad.</p>		\n			<a href=\"#\">\n									DOWNLOAD\n					</a>\n													<img width=\"811\" height=\"924\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads.webp 811w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-263x300.webp 263w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-768x875.webp 768w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/group-of-cws-ads-600x684.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 811px) 100vw, 811px\" />','File Prep','','inherit','closed','closed','','17743-revision-v1','','','2024-08-28 11:03:17','2024-08-28 11:03:17','',17743,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=17777',0,'revision','',0),(17778,2,'2024-08-28 11:03:17','2024-08-28 11:03:17','<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=\".svg\"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>										<img width=\"978\" height=\"978\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates.webp 978w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-300x300.webp 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/printing-comics-is-helping-you-set-up-your-comic-book-size-with-our-templates-150x150.webp 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/p