elementor-widget-heading .elementor-heading-title.elementor-size-xxl{font-size:59px}</style><h2>Who We Are</h2>		\n		<p>Printing Comics is a premier digital printing company located in Merrillville, Indiana, specializing in end-to-end Comic Book printing services. Founded in 2024 as a commercial and dedicated comic book printer, we print comic books for select individuals across the country.  We were founded as a result of an attempt of censorship by Ready Comics and Brian Pulido and are a sister company of Divinity Comics Inc.  Our primary goal is to maintain Divinity Comics\' industry presence and help fellow creators find a cheaper more economical solution for their printing needs.</p>		\n			<h2>What We Do</h2>		\n		<p>That\'s simple, we print comics.</p>		\n			<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image-box .elementor-image-box-content{width:100%}@media (min-width:768px){.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-position-left .elementor-image-box-wrapper,.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-position-right .elementor-image-box-wrapper{display:flex}.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-position-right .elementor-image-box-wrapper{text-align:end;flex-direction:row-reverse}.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-position-left .elementor-image-box-wrapper{text-align:start;flex-direction:row}.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-position-top .elementor-image-box-img{margin:auto}.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-vertical-align-top .elementor-image-box-wrapper{align-items:flex-start}.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-vertical-align-middle .elementor-image-box-wrapper{align-items:center}.elementor-widget-image-box.elementor-vertical-align-bottom .elementor-image-box-wrapper{align-items:flex-end}}@media (max-width:767px){.elementor-widget-image-box .elementor-image-box-img{margin-left:auto!important;margin-right:auto!important;margin-bottom:15px}}.elementor-widget-image-box .elementor-image-box-img{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image-box .elementor-image-box-title a{color:inherit}.elementor-widget-image-box .elementor-image-box-wrapper{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image-box .elementor-image-box-description{margin:0}</style><figure><img width=\"59\" height=\"59\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/target.webp\" alt=\"\" /></figure><h3>Our Mission</h3><p>At Printing Comics, it is our mission to retain standard at all levels from our product and service quality to customer’s satisfaction. We love and value our customers and aim to deliver our promise; premium comic books printing and unmatched customer’s service that is almost impossible to find anywhere even outside the industry.</p>		\n			<figure><img width=\"59\" height=\"59\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/vision.webp\" alt=\"\" /></figure><h3>Our Vision</h3><p>To become a one-stop comic printing shop leveraging years of printing experience and expertise in meticulously delivering every project. We want to be globally recognized as one of a kind digital printing company - exceptional in its printing accuracy and precision.</p>		\n			<figure><img width=\"59\" height=\"59\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/values.webp\" alt=\"\" /></figure><h3>Our Values</h3><p>Integrity, honesty, great quality, and swift turn around times. These are more than taglines for us: they are the key pillars holding our business right from its formation. We relate with every customer keeping these words as our guiding principles. Our ability to embody these values in everything that we do is what truly set us apart from others.</p>		\n			<figure><img width=\"59\" height=\"59\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/customer-service.webp\" alt=\"\" /></figure><h3>Customer Service</h3><p>At the heart of Printing Comics is a commitment to continually foster a strong relationship with you, answering your queries concerning our services, and maintaining our core values, keeping current with changing trends, and competitors. Here, we don’t just meet your needs; we surpass them. Get in touch today and let\'s make your overall experience as enjoyable as possible!</p>		\n			<style>/*! elementor - v3.23.0 - 05-08-2024 */\n.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=\".svg\"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>										<img width=\"606\" height=\"606\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31.png 606w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-300x300.png 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-150x150.png 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-600x600.png 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 606px) 100vw, 606px\" />													\n													<img width=\"606\" height=\"606\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31.png 606w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-300x300.png 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-150x150.png 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-600x600.png 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 606px) 100vw, 606px\" />													\n													<img width=\"606\" height=\"606\" src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31.png 606w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-300x300.png 300w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-150x150.png 150w, https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/elip-sale-31-600x600.png 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 606px) 100vw, 606px\" />													\n			<h2>Ready to buy in bulk & save up to 50%?</h2>		\n			<h2>Printed and shipped on demand!</h2>		\n        		<a role=\"button\" href=\"/shop\">\n								Shop Now\n			    			</a>','About Us','','inherit','closed','closed','','9462-revision-v1','','','2024-09-10 05:22:19','2024-09-10 05:22:19','',9462,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=19649',0,'revision','',0),(19650,1,'2024-09-10 05:30:17','2024-09-10 05:30:17','','Screenshot 2024-09-10 002704','','inherit','open','closed','','screenshot-2024-09-10-002704','','','2024-09-10 05:30:17','2024-09-10 05:30:17','',57,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Screenshot-2024-09-10-002704.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(19651,1,'2024-09-10 05:33:54','2024-09-10 05:33:54','<ul>\n 	<li><strong>Staple binding</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Interior page counts from 8-64 - 25 minimum quantity print</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Rush delivery is available</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Price Breaks with higher quantities</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Wide variety of cover &amp; interiors paper options</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Full color OR Black &amp; White (includes grayscale)</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Printing templates available!</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Printing Comics AD insert discount option</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Foil cover instructions</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Reordering Note:</strong></h2>\n<strong>For reprints/reorders of comic books over four months old, sending us a physical copy of the previous version helps ensure color consistency. Please reach out to customer service (sales@mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980) if you have questions regarding shipping costs for this process. We DO NOT keep files on hand for more than 12 months. If you have not placed an order in over 12 months, you must share your files with us.</strong>\n<h2>Variant Covers</h2>\n<strong>Separate Line Items</strong>: Different stocks or interiors (even one page) are not considered variants and must be ordered as separate line items. This includes sketch covers, foils, etc.\n\n<strong>Minimum Order Quantities</strong>:\n<ul>\n 	<li>For true variants, submit the interior files once and each cover individually, labeled clearly.</li>\n 	<li>Indicate quantities of each variant in the notes section. Each variant must be ordered in a minimum of 10 copies.</li>\n 	<li>Specialty orders (e.g., foils) require no minimum.</li>\n 	<li>When placing your order, you can upload variant cover files and signify the details in the notes section.</li>\n</ul>\nPlease make sure to label the covers CLEARLY and indicate in the notes how many of each.\n<h2>Saddle Stitch Binding</h2>\nThe saddle stitch is a popular book binding method used by publishers worldwide. Commercial publishers and booklet makers use this popular binding method to create magazines, pamphlets, brochures, catalogs, coloring books, and short comics.\n<h2>What is Saddle Stitch Binding?</h2>\nSaddle stitching uses two special book binding staples to secure the book together. Printers use a saddle stapler or stitching machine to bind loose pages together.\n\nTwo large staples are placed into the fold of the paper. The stapler pushes the staples through sheets of paper and clamps them shut. The sheets of paper are then folded, creating a saddle-stitched booklet.\n\nSaddle-stitched books use several sheets of paper folded and printed on the front and back. For this reason, saddle stitching books must have page counts in multiples of 4. For example, a saddle stitch binding page count could be 28 pages, but not 26.\n\nSaddle stitching is a good choice for 64 pages or shorter books. They are also perfect for shorter soft cover books like mini-comic books or comics series with short issues. An excellent example of saddle-stick comics is the original DC comics like Batman from the 1930s, 40s, and 50s.\n\nHigher page counts, especially final page counts above 100 pages, are too difficult to staple together in this way. Instead, longer books may use square binding, which creates a flat, square spine.\n<h2>How is Saddle Stitch Binding Different from Perfect Binding?</h2>\nSaddle-stitched books differ from <a href=\"https://printingcomics.com/product/novels-square-bound-paperbacks-glue-binding/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">perfect binding</a> in a few keyways. Instead of staples, perfecting binding uses glue to secure the pages together. In this book binding process, printed pages are grouped together in a book block. The book block is then glued to a cover with a spine.\n\nPerfect binding is ideal for longer graphic novels, books with a large, finished size, and books that need a printable spine. Perfect binding is also known as square binding and can give a softcover book a more professional appearance; however, it is the more expensive book binding choice.\n<h2>When to Use Saddle Stitch Binding</h2>\nSaddle stitch is the best binding technique for shorter comic books between 8 and 64 pages. This is because it is generally limited to 16 sheets of paper. Including the covers and inside covers, 64 pages create a total count of 68 pages maximum for the book.\n<h2>Staple Binding with Comix Well Spring</h2>\nPrinting Comics offers professional printing and binding comic book services. Our staple binding option focuses on convenience, quality, and fast turnaround so that you can receive your finished project in no time.\n<h3>Paper type</h3>\nSaddle stitch booklets from Printing Comics use 60# bright white paper on the inside and 80# glossy paper for the front and back cover. Sketch covers are available with 80# matte Bristol board. Both are cost-effective options with strong wire staples that allow your readers to enjoy your work.\n<h3>Print time</h3>\nDigital printing service turnaround for saddle stitch binding is two weeks, but we offer faster options if needed. Our comic service can accommodate your timelines, even if you need a large custom-bound comics order quickly. Simply let us know when you order, and we will work with you to get your comic printed on time.\n<h2>How to Place Your Saddle Stitch Order</h2>\nTo place your saddle stitch book order with Printing Comics, upload your black and white or full-color comic pages using our easy ordering system. Follow the prompts and choose your number of pages, paper type, and color option.\n\nMake sure your upload is in 300 dpi resolution. Also, ensure that each file is formatted exactly as you want it to print and labeled with its page number.\n\nLet us know whether you want a digital proof or physical proof and check it carefully to ensure your full-color comic book printing and margins show up correctly. Once everything looks perfect, let us know, and we’ll get printing.\n\nYou should receive your order in under two weeks.\n<h2>Choose Saddle Stitch Binding for Your Comic Book</h2>\nIf you are printing a comic book, pamphlet, brochure, or coloring book, choose Printing Comics for your printing needs. Our saddle stitch binding and print services will ensure that your product looks professional and lasts in the hands of your readers. We also offer perfect-bound books for longer projects.\n\nTo learn more about how comic books are printed or ask questions about choosing the correct format and print setting for your project, contact our customer service team or check out our free resources. We can answer any questions you have about saddle stitch and print options.','Comics - Saddle stitch (staple binding)','For reprints/reorders of comic books over four months old, sending us a physical copy of the previous version helps ensure color consistency. Please reach out to customer service (sales@mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980) if you have questions regarding shipping costs for this process. We DO NOT keep files on hand for more than 12 months. If you have not placed an order in over 12 months, you must share your files with us.','inherit','closed','closed','','57-autosave-v1','','','2024-09-10 05:33:54','2024-09-10 05:33:54','',57,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=19651',0,'revision','',0),(19652,1,'2024-09-10 05:34:55','2024-09-10 05:34:55','','Screenshot 2024-09-10 002910','','inherit','open','closed','','screenshot-2024-09-10-002910','','','2024-09-10 05:34:55','2024-09-10 05:34:55','',64,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Screenshot-2024-09-10-002910.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(19653,1,'2024-09-10 05:40:57','2024-09-10 05:40:57','<ul>\n 	<li><strong>Perfect bound (glue binding) - square</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Interior page counts from 20-300 (</strong><strong>*If page count exceeds 300 email for quote)</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>NO minimum quantity print</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Rush delivery is available</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Price Breaks with higher quantities</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Wide variety of cover &amp; interiors paper options</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Full color OR Black &amp; White (includes grayscale)</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Printing templates available!</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Printing Comics AD insert discount option</strong></li>\n 	<li><strong>Foil cover instructions</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<strong>*Spine width formula: Use our new Printing Comics spine width calculator here!</strong>\n<h2><strong>Reordering Note:</strong></h2>\n<strong>For reprints/reorders of comic books over four months old, sending us a physical copy of the previous version helps ensure color consistency. Please reach out to customer service (sales@printingcomics.com) if you have questions regarding shipping costs for this process. We DO NOT keep files on hand for more than 12 months. If you have not placed an order in over 12 months, you must share your files with us.</strong>\n<h2>Variant Covers</h2>\n<strong>Separate Line Items</strong>: Different stocks or interiors (even one page) are not considered variants and must be ordered as separate line items. This includes sketch covers, foils, etc.\n\n<strong>Minimum Order Quantities</strong>:\n<ul>\n 	<li>For true variants, submit the interior files once and each cover individually, labeled clearly.</li>\n 	<li>Indicate quantities of each variant in the notes section.</li>\n 	<li>Specialty orders (e.g., foils) require NO minimum.</li>\n 	<li>When placing your order, you can upload variant cover files and signify the details in the notes section.</li>\n</ul>\nPlease make sure to label the covers CLEARLY and indicate in the notes how many of each.\n<h2>Graphic Novel Printing</h2>\nNo matter what genre of graphic novel or comic you’re creating, the final print size and quality have a huge impact on your readers’ experience. Whether you’re a veteran with a large following or a new artist trying to break into indie comics, you’ll need the best printing team on your side.\n\nPrinting Comics specializes in comic book and graphic novel printing. We offer perfect bound books and saddle stitched comics custom printed in black and white or vibrant color. We offer multiple book sizes and can even create custom sizes so you can tell your story however you see fit.\n<h3>Which Binding Is Best for Graphic Novels?</h3>\nComic books tend to be serialized, while graphic novels are almost always wrapped up in one or two volumes. By definition, graphic novels tend to be longer than the 64-page maximum allowed by <a href=\"https://printingcomics.com/product/comics-saddle-stitch-staple-binding/\">saddle stitching binding</a>. Square binding is a much better option, as it allows page counts of 260 or more.\n\nBoth binding options are very durable, and can last for years when used with the right paper and ink. However, square stitching looks more professional. It also allows room for printing the novel’s title on the spine, which helps readers find it more easily.\n<h3>Paper Quality and Type for Square Bound Paperbacks</h3>\nAt Printing Comics, we use 60# bright white paper for the inside of our saddle stitched and square bound books. This paper is bright enough to keep your illustrations highly visible, and thick enough to hold up through years of re-reading.\n\nWe offer Standard, Foil, and sketch covers. Standard covers are glossy 80# paper, which has a good balance of durability and low cost. Sketch covers use 80# paper with a matte finish to allow them to be drawn on easily.\n\nGraphic novels can use any of the three cover types. If you regularly visit conventions, a sketch cover is a great investment for fans who want something they can get signed and customized.\n<h3>Full Color or Black and White</h3>\nFull color and black and white comics offer dramatically different final results. Black and white is perfect for horror stories, gritty detective stories, or other narratives that rely heavily on shadows and textures. Black and white printing can also handle grayscale, which is great for everything from manga to minimalist memoirs.\n\nAlthough full color is more expensive than black and white printing, it’s well worth it for high-action genres with heavy worldbuilding. Books with black and white interiors still include color covers, so you can show off and entice readers with your full-color art.\n\nThe best option for your graphic novel depends on your own art style and budget. If you put the work into creating a full-color graphic novel, make it available to your fans with our affordable full-color printing. Black and white and grayscale artists can still develop a huge following, partly thanks to the lower printing costs.\n<h3>Book Sizes</h3>\nThe standard comic book printed size is 6.625″ x 10.25”, magazine size is 8” x 10.5”, and manga size is 5.5″ x 7.75″. All three sizes require final art that is slightly larger than the page size, to allow for trimming.\n\nManga size may be an option for artists who use fewer panels per page or have less detailed art. It’s also a good way to keep costs as low as possible, regardless of the length of your printing project.\n\nGraphic novels tend to be longer than comic books, so larger magazine size books may not be cost-effective. However, this can be highly variable depending on ink color and overall length. We’re happy to answer any questions you have about length, size, and ink possibilities. Whatever you decide, make sure to use the correct comic page template for formatting your final product.\n<h3>Support from Start to Finish</h3>\nNo matter what kind of comic book or graphic novel you’ve created, Comix Well Spring can help get you through the final step of printing. Our perfect binding books have reliable turnaround time, with standard printing taking two weeks after proofs are approved. We also offer faster printing and express shipping if needed to meet your deadline.\n\nOur customer service team knows about the process of creating and publishing comics, so they can answer any questions you have about <a href=\"https://www.grekoprinting-comixwellspring.com/\">comic book printing</a>, formatting, and shipping. Join us as you embark on your next artistic adventure.','Novels - Square Bound Paperbacks (Glue Binding)','','inherit','closed','closed','','64-autosave-v1','','','2024-09-10 05:40:57','2024-09-10 05:40:57','',64,'https://mhc.lxf.temporary.site/website_b3635980/?p=19653',0,'revision','',0),(19654,1,'2024-09-10 06:35:35','2024-09-10 06:35:35','<a href=\"https://printingcomics.com/\">\n	<img src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/printing-comics.png\" alt=\"Printing Comics - \">\n	<img src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/printing-comics.png\" alt=\"Printing Comics - \">\n	<img src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/printing-comics.png\" alt=\"Printing Comics - \">\n	<img src=\"https://printingcomics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/printing-comics.png\" alt=\"Printing Comics - \">\n</a>\n